# TPOWER Global Visual System

The **Games page** (`/[locale]/games`) is the visual quality benchmark for the entire website.

Every page must feel like one premium product — not an independent landing page.

## Canonical building blocks

- `AtmosphereHero` / upgraded `PageHeader` — full-bleed atmosphere image, dark overlay, red radial, fade to black
- `AtmosphereMedia` — every photo/illustration uses gradient blending (never a hard rectangle)
- `PremiumCta` — left copy + buttons, right blended artwork (never empty)
- `ProvidersMarquee` via `ProvidersMarqueeSlot` in `SiteShell` — site-wide above the footer

## Hero rules

- Large full-width background image
- Dark overlay + large radial red gradient
- Smooth fade to black — no hard image edges
- Image = atmosphere, not a banner

## Image rules

Stack treatment on every image:

1. Image
2. Dark overlay
3. Radial gradient
4. Fade into page background

## CTA rules

Follow Games CTA / `PremiumCta`:

- Left ~58%: headline, description, buttons
- Right ~42%: high-quality illustration (phone, casino, promo, product)
- Never leave the right side empty

## Provider marquee

Site-wide branding element above the footer:

- Single row, infinite scroll
- Colored logos always visible
- No grayscale-only / hover-to-reveal
- Responsive spacing and logo size

## Section rhythm

Alternate content ↔ visual ↔ statistics ↔ CTA. Avoid long text-only blocks.

## Spacing & surfaces

- Large section padding
- Rounded containers
- Dark cards, subtle borders, soft shadows
- Red accent gradients

## Responsive (desktop-first)

Desktop is the master composition. Mobile must **scale** the same layout — not restack, reorder, or simplify.

See `tpower-desktop-first-responsive.mdc` (always apply). Prefer `overflow-x-auto` card rows and persistent multi-column grids over `flex-col` / `grid-cols-1` breakpoints.

## Philosophy
Apple / Stripe / Linear / Vercel premium SaaS **plus** high-end casino branding.

Avoid: cheap casino templates, gold everywhere, flashing neon, AI-looking layouts, overcrowded sections.

## Completion gate

A page is not complete until it matches Games-page quality. If a page looks older than Games, redesign it to this system before shipping.
